* ==== END DUT ====

* ---- bench: kickback (klt sim port of sim/comparator-kickback) ----------
*
* Circuit is sim/comparator-kickback/testbench/tb_kickback.spice's, carried
* over element for element (branch A: 1 kohm / 100 fF; branches B/C: 1 Gohm
* / 1 pF floating inputs at 1 mV and 100 mV), with two changes:
*
* 1. SUPPLY-TRACKING CLOCK. klt sim sweeps supply by `alter vsup=<V>`, which
*    does not reach the original `pulse(0 {vdd_val} ...)` amplitude, so the
*    strobe here is a unit pulse scaled by the live supply node (Bclk) --
*    same timing, rail-to-rail at every supply corner.
*
* 2. A DIRECT Q_kick MEASUREMENT on branch A, which DR-0002 Row 4 names as an
*    open item ("A direct Q_kick measurement in the kickback bench"). The
*    original deck emits no charge at all; DR-0002 Row 4 (b) shows the only
*    available estimator (peak volts x C_in) under-reports by ~1.3-2.9x.
*    Here each branch-A DUT input pin is reached through a 0 V ammeter
*    (vkp / vkn), so i(vkp) is exactly the DUT + input pin's own current.
*    A behavioural current source integrates it onto a 1 pF capacitor
*    (Bqp -> qp), so v(qp) [V] x 1000 is the running pin charge in fC. Sign:
*    oriented so that v(qp) RISES when the DUT pushes charge INTO node apa
*    (checked in the single-corner smoke: v(qp) - v(qp)@29ns peaks positive
*    in the same window where v(ad) = v(apa) - v(asp) peaks positive). The
*    sign does not enter the graded number, which is an absolute value. The
*    request measures v(qp) at 29 ns (DR-0002's pre-decision reference) and
*    its max/min over the 30 ... 45 ns window, so
*        Q_kick = max_t |q(t) - q(29 ns)|,  t in [30 ns, 45 ns]
*    which is DR-0002 Row 4's definition `max_t |int i_kick dt'|` verbatim.
*    The ammeters are ideal 0 V sources and the integrators load nothing,
*    so the circuit the DUT sees is the original one. Rqp only gives the
*    integrator node a DC path: tau = 1 ms (~10^5 x the 15 ns window), and
*    small enough that the pin's DC leakage parks v(qp) at only mV, so the
*    6-significant-figure .meas print keeps sub-0.001 fC resolution.

.options reltol=1e-4 vntol=1e-9 abstol=1e-15 chgtol=1e-16

.param rsrc=1k
.param cin=100f
.param rfloat=1G
.param cfloat=1p
.param dv_small=1m
.param dv_big=100m

vsup vdd 0 dc 1.2
vcm  cm 0 dc {dut_vcm}

* One strobe at 30 ns, as in the original (`pulse(0 {vdd_val} 30n 100p
* 100p 10n 30n)`), scaled by the altered supply.
vclku clku 0 pulse(0 1 30n 100p 100p 10n 30n)
Bclk  clk  0 v = 'v(clku)*v(vdd)'

* ---- A: 1 kohm source impedance (DR-0002 Row 4's stated condition) ------
vsa  sa 0 dc {dv_small}
Easp asp cm sa 0 0.5
Easn asn cm sa 0 -0.5
Rap  asp apa {rsrc}
Ran  asn ana {rsrc}
Cap  apa 0 {cin}
Can  ana 0 {cin}
* 0 V ammeters into the DUT pins (new; see header item 2)
vkp  apa apa_pin dc 0
vkn  ana ana_pin dc 0
iba  vdd ibna dc {dut_ib}
Xa   apa_pin ana_pin clk ibna douta doutba vdd 0 comparator_dut

* ---- branch-A injected-charge integrators (new; see header item 2) ------
Bqp  0 qp i = 'i(vkp)'
Cqp  qp 0 1p
Rqp  qp 0 1e9
Bqn  0 qn i = 'i(vkn)'
Cqn  qn 0 1p
Rqn  qn 0 1e9

* ---- B: floating high-Z input, small residue ----------------------------
vsb  sb 0 dc {dv_small}
Ebsp bsp cm sb 0 0.5
Ebsn bsn cm sb 0 -0.5
Rbp  bsp bpp {rfloat}
Rbn  bsn bpn {rfloat}
Cbp  bpp 0 {cfloat}
Cbn  bpn 0 {cfloat}
ibb  vdd ibnb dc {dut_ib}
Xb   bpp bpn clk ibnb doutb doutbb vdd 0 comparator_dut

* ---- C: floating high-Z input, large residue ----------------------------
vsc  sc 0 dc {dv_big}
Ecsp csp cm sc 0 0.5
Ecsn csn cm sc 0 -0.5
Rcp  csp cpp {rfloat}
Rcn  csn cpn {rfloat}
Ccp  cpp 0 {cfloat}
Ccn  cpn 0 {cfloat}
ibc  vdd ibnc dc {dut_ib}
Xc   cpp cpn clk ibnc doutc doutbc vdd 0 comparator_dut

* ---- near-zero-referenced probes (as in the original) -------------------
Bad ad 0 v = 'v(apa)-v(asp)'
Bbd bd 0 v = 'v(bpp)-v(bpn)'
Bcd cd 0 v = 'v(cpp)-v(cpn)'
Bbc bc 0 v = '(v(bpp)+v(bpn))/2-v(cm)'

* ---- supply-normalized decision probes ----------------------------------
Bdan dan 0 v = 'v(douta)/v(vdd)'
Bdbn dbn 0 v = 'v(doutb)/v(vdd)'
Bdcn dcn 0 v = 'v(doutc)/v(vdd)'

* ---- corner-application probe (see regeneration bench) ------------------
Btchk tcheck 0 v = 'temper'
